  "notes": "The songwriter-producer who rebuilt female pop stars around vintage tone and analogue programming: 92–130 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the ballads at 66–80. The drum block is documented as an outsider's: she \"**programmed her first dance track while teaching herself drum programming**, and the result is intentionally non-drummerly\". Three deltas follow: \"kick on 1 and 3 plus an 8th pickup\" (second anchor \"4&\"), \"a big **front-loaded** snare on 2&4\" — which is the highest accent tier here against an ordinary main, the numeric reading of front-loading — and \"horn samples used as percussive accents\", which is why the perc block is `perc`-led rather than shaker-led. Harmony is B minor / G major with i–VI–III–VII for the anthems and I–V–vi–IV for the ballads, \"piano-voiced with added 9ths, and a deliberately 'wrong' chord or instrument left in the arrangement as a signature\" — the ninths are authored at 0.2 and the deliberate wrongness is the raised `halfStepDissonance`. She plays the bass herself: \"fat, mono, root-based 8ths; on the new-wave-leaning material a synth-bass riff *is* the hook\", which is why `followRootsProb` sits at 0.85 rather than locked. Her ballads \"build from solo piano to a full band by chorus 2 **with no key change**\", so the lift is in the arrangement. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 110.",
